dy, along with a number of useful home recipea, instructions and patterns of various kinds of tau': work. SS weldon's Ladies' Journal" includes two Cli„t",..°ll patterns of popular, and fashionable garments 7 Victoria Cape," and "New Zouave Bodice. Weldon's patterns are always easy to iollow,and rellntui;, the description of them giving particulars as to ci of material, &amp;c., and instructions as to putting uathe° together. otity of " Weldon's Practical Needlework" gives a clua made useful, and pretty designs of articles easily to bfe tourerY of" Crinkled Paper." The variety of shadeso c' in this paper, now so extensively used, ancl.!_h: v to reasonable price of it, enable any one so inclined, make artistic knick-knacks for very little money. The Public Ans CADBURY'S COCOA is a bsolutely Pur— tests /yets have submitted CADBURY:EI COCOA to and the result has always proved its great 'MUM a ag Sad &amp;wishing heveraga, —Advt.</p>
