        <p>CEMETERY COMETITT'ES.—" I.NCR OVSYTSINEFS.* Alderman HAMMON, in Rtveing the adoption of the Cemetery Committee's minutes, saia that they were going on Rs well as they °avid expect. They wets bury- ing as few people as they possibly ,crald, and be hoped they would bury still less. Councillor ASHTON seconded tira motion and the minutes were adopted. They curtained the report of the Registrar which Etriwed tbat the interments for tht past month were adults, 33 ; minors, 50•; 136.111 born and premature, H. Corresponding period last.year, adults 53 ; minors, 4f9 ; stillborn and premature, 9. The ^re- ceipts for the month were £13.511-s. against :277 10s. lest year.</p>
