        <head>PARADISE FOR MINISTERS.</head>
        <p>A PARADISE FOR MINISTERS.</p>
        <p>--- The " Boston Herald" says :—" It is usually said that there is no paradise for ministers until they enter the other world ; but in Brooklyn some of them at least find themselves in paradise while they are still in this world. The Brooklyn people know how to treat their pastors well. Their traditions are good on this point, and the recent present to Dr. Berhends of a cheque for £6OO and to Dr. Lyman tsf a similar checine for £1,400, shows that good men in that locality are not without I their reward in the filthy lucre of this world. In this I case what is given is the savour of the prayers as well as the good wishes of the donors, and it is not surpris- ing that the Brooklyn ministers have long pastorates and grow old gracefully when their duties have fallen to them in places where faithful services are well appre- ciated.</p>
